From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:23:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 251/294] gallium/pvr: compile the milestone-2 vertex shader
 from SPIR-V through spirv_to_nir

The probe's vertex shader now comes from a SPIR-V module (an Input vec3 at location 0 and a plain
Output vec4 decorated BuiltIn Position, assembled with spirv-as) parsed by spirv_to_nir with
pco_spirv_options()/pco_nir_options() - the same path the Vulkan driver uses - instead of NIR built by
hand. pco compiles it to a 56-byte USC program with temps=0, vtxins=3 and vtxouts=5: the attribute load
survives and the register allocator no longer aborts, and the byte-identical-to-constant-shader check
still passes. The glslang form that wraps gl_Position in the gl_PerVertex interface block trips
nir_split_per_member_structs() in this pco build (segfault inside build_member_deref), so the module uses
a plain Output variable - the shape pco's own lowering produces.

Also link idep_vtn for the probe and make its stdout unbuffered (crash reports stay readable).
pvr-probe --- ALL PASS (shim), and the same path runs on the real driver.
